    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement is that membership level 4 requires tenure of more than 365 days, and a newly created owner (zero tenure) can never exceed level 3.\n\nI confined the change to the single small `OwnerMembershipLevelPolicy` class (one file, one edited method plus one tiny cohesive helper):\n\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) still cap at 3 via `Math.min`.\n- Level 4 is only unlocked when an owner is already at that cap of 3 **and** tenure exceeds 365 days:\n  ```java\n  return level == MAX_LEVEL && exceedsTenure(owner.getRegistrationDate()) ? level + 1 : level;\n  ```\n- A new `exceedsTenure` helper computes days since `registrationDate`. Since a new owner's registration date is today, tenure is 0, so a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 (and any household size) lands at level 3, never 4 \u2014 exactly as specified.\n\nStructural impact was kept minimal: the edited class has essentially no other complexity (WMC_other \u2248 1), the changed method stays simple, and only one file was touched. The acceptance test (`coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`) and the full suite pass.",
